WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.433
Will Trump in

00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:00.967
Fulton County,

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:04.270
prosecutors have agreed on a $200,000

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:05.338
cash bond

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:06.106
just ahead

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:07.607
of his expected surrender

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:10.143
at the Fulton County Jail on Thursday.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.711
We're now told it will be Thursday.

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:13.246
Brian Todd is taking a closer

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:15.482
look into this into this jail for us.

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:16.449
What can you tell us

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:17.517
about the former president

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:18.451
as co-defendants

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:20.153
when they actually show up there

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:21.021
what they can expect?

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:22.288
Wolf, according to the Fulton County

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.523
sheriff, is to be treated

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.658
like any other defendant at that jail.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.560
But we do have new information tonight

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:28.461
on how the process

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:29.629
could be streamlined

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:30.463
for Donald Trump

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:32.565
and the other defendants.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:33.900
Donald Trump,

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:34.901
Rudy Giuliani

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.770
and 17 other defendants

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:37.904
this week are expected

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.005
to be formally booked

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:40.640
at the Fulton County Jail,

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.510
also known as Rice Street, a hulking

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:44.644
crumbling structure

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:46.713
that's garnered a notorious reputation.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:48.782
The sheriff of Fulton County

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:50.417
insisting that despite their high

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:51.484
profiles, Trump

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.719
and the others will be treated

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:54.120
like every other defendant

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.321
booked at this jail.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.589
If you're indicted,

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:57.490
then we're going to treat you

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.726
as though you indicted here locally.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.728
And so we will continue to

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.830
do fingerprints, mug shots, etc.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.865
What might it look like inside when Trump

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:07.667
and the others formally surrender?

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.135
Retired Fulton County Sheriff's

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:09.936
Lieutenant Charles

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:11.805
Rambo says normally people

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:12.639
who are surrendering

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:13.740
come through the facility's

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.208
front door first.

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.243
But regardless of which entrances Trump

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.511
and the others arrive in.

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.713
They would be pat down,

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:23.183
led to the booking office in the rear.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.884
From there,

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:27.320
they probably will have to have ties

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.221
and shoestrings

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:30.857
and all those type of things taken.

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:34.094
Then from there, the persons would be

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:38.665
fingerprinted, given a booking photo.

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:39.666
Donald Trump

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:41.301
and the other defendants are expected

00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:42.035
to be photographed

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:42.936
for mug shots,

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:44.771
but it's unclear when those pictures

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:45.972
will be made public.

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.640
People familiar with the process tell

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.642
CNN normally those booked at

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.344
this jail are searched thoroughly

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:52.612
by a jail deputy,

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:53.446
and at some point,

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:55.248
given a medical examination

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.916
and a pretrial screening

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:57.584
to determine

00:01:57.584 --> 00:01:58.551
if they can sign out

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.253
on their own recognizance.

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:01.187
But it's not clear

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:02.288
if Trump or the other high

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.190
profile defendants in this case

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.292
will go through those steps.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:07.560
For a normal defendant,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.728
it would take hours to go

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:09.896
through those procedures.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:11.297
But with these defendants,

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:12.465
I don't expect Trump

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:13.700
to spend hours in this jail,

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.902
because the longer he is

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:16.769
I mean, it's a pain.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:19.372
It's going to be a hassle for the entire

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:20.773
sheriff's department,

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:22.208
or at least those that are at the jail

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:22.909
when the president

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:24.310
is there going to be a circus?

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.079
If they didn't have bond agreements?

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:26.813
Donald Trump

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:27.947
and the other defendants

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.883
might have been held in custody at this

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:30.517
jail,

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:31.217
which observers

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:33.419
say could be a nightmarish experience.

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:34.287
The rice free

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:35.889
jail is not a pleasant place.

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:38.024
It's dirty It's scary.

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:38.858
Last month,

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:39.859
the Justice Department

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:41.628
launched a civil rights investigation

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:43.163
into the Fulton County Jail

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:44.564
following multiple deaths

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:46.132
inside the facility

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:46.799
last year,

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:48.101
inmate Lashaun Thompson

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:49.936
was found dead in his cell.

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:52.205
His family says unsanitary conditions,

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:54.774
including insect and lice infestation,

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:56.609
contributed to his death.

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:59.012
Even the sheriff agree

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.780
it was deplorable conditions like

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.550
a third world country.

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:05.818
Three officials of the

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.187
Fulton County Jail stepped down

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:08.288
earlier this year

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:09.923
after a preliminary investigation

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:11.691
into Lashaun Thompson's death.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:13.493
Sheriff Patrick Labonte acknowledges

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:14.761
the poor conditions there.

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:15.695
He says he welcomes

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:17.497
the Justice Department investigation

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:18.198
and he has sought

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:20.066
more than $2 billion in county

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:22.202
funding to build a new jail Wolf.

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:23.736
Horrendous situation over there.

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:25.572
Thanks very much, Brian Todd reporting

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:26.406
I want to bring in

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:27.106
CNN legal

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:28.875
analyst Norm Eisen for more on

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:30.376
the breaking news we're following.

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:31.077
The breaking news

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:32.645
that the former president, Donald Trump,

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:34.280
will turn himself in

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.915
to authorities down in Georgia

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.183
on Thursday.

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:39.452
What's your reaction to him?

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:40.853
Well, Wolf,

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:41.821
despite the fact

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:43.690
that we've seen this before,

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.091
there is no denying

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:47.560
the historic nature of it

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.796
even to have one

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:52.999
surrender one time by a president.

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:54.901
Now, the fourth time

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.236
These are some of the most

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:57.270
serious charges

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.004
he faces

00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:00.240
with some of the most serious penalties.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.374
But we also have to be

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:03.176
cognizant, Wolf, of the ways

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:05.445
in which the former president

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.747
is utilizing the spectacle

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:09.549
of these surrenders

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:11.217
and the related

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:13.519
appearances, the arrangements

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.488
to drive his support

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:17.557
and his popularity in the Republican

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:19.859
presidential primaries.

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:21.294
So we're seeing that

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:22.729
and we can expect that as well.

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:23.396
On Thursday,

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:25.398
if he were just a regular citizen

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:26.833
and he was facing these

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.067
criminal charges,

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.636
he'd not only be fingerprinted,

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:30.903
but have a mug shot.

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.372
But presumably,

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:33.906
they could deny him even bail.

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:34.507
Right.

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:37.176
They could.

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:41.814
I think most regular citizens who were

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:45.184
who had no history of conviction,

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:46.919
he has multiple criminal charges,

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:49.322
but he has not been convicted,

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:52.091
would be eligible either for bail

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:53.960
or for a bond of the kind

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.428
that he's posting here.

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:57.330
We know that also from the treatment

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.798
of his co-defendants.

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:00.033
But we do expect that

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:02.068
some of the usual strictures

00:05:02.068 --> 00:05:05.672
in this jail, which is not a

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:08.341
very nice place to be.

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:11.344
Some of the usual strictures

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:13.046
will be relaxed to move him

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:14.080
in and out quickly.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.149
We've seen that in the prior arrest,

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:17.984
the prior surrenders.

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:19.452
And we'll see that here, too.

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:19.952
And, of course,

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:22.889
the Secret Service is negotiating that.

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:24.390
That is a security concern.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.225
So for that reason alone,

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:27.460
because he'll have

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.662
a strong accompaniment, strong security,

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:31.030
he'll have a very different

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.999
experience than the normal defendant.

